Date: Tue, 12 Jan 93 22:01:49 EST
From: pmetzger@shearson.com (Perry E. Metzger)
Subject: Re: EVOL New Genes

> From: David Jevans <jevans@apple.com>
> 
> I wonder what new genes will come into effect in human evolution given
> the vastly different environment that we live in.  There are likely numerous
> genes for intellectualism, understanding of complex mathematics and large
> systems, dynamism, etc. that will determine who migrates to the trans-human
> stage.  These could be long dormant genes that have been irrelevant to
> previous evolution.

I think we've passed the end of evolution involving DNA. The next major step
in human development is likely to be the abandonment of our current bodies
entirely, and their DNA with them. We are passing beyond slow biological
evolution into the transhuman stage where change will occur as a result of
intentional design and competition rather than random genetic mutation
and competition. "Genes", especially old ones that are no longer biologically
active, will likely cease to exist and be replaced with blueprints and
the moral equivalent -- the triumph of the meme over the gene.

Perry

